<title>GERMANY: THYSSEN SAYS TRANSRAPID PROJECT TO CONTINUE.</title>
<headline>THYSSEN SAYS TRANSRAPID PROJECT TO CONTINUE.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>German steel and engineering group Thyssen AG said on Friday that Germany's Transrapid rail project would continue despite confirmation from one of the construction groups involved that the building firms involved were quitting the project.</p>
<p>A Thyssen spokesman told Reuters the departure of the construction groups, which include Philipp Holzmann AG and Hochtief, the country's two largest, would better secure financing for the project.</p>
</text>
